Prof.V.Rama Rao

Prof.V.Rama Rao presently Consultant to Center for Good Governance, has passed his B.Tech. from JNTU in Electrical Engg. ME in Industrial Drives and Controlled from OU. He has done PG Diploma in Computer Science& Engg., MHRD, Chennai. He has Foreign Fellowship Training Programme in Robotics andCAD/CAM from NMIT, Australia. D.Sc. ( Electrical Engineering )from US. He received the Best Teacher Award from ISTE in 1998 and Best Principal Award from Govt of AP in 2002. Prof. Rao has about 41 years of Industrial, Professional and Academic experience. He has started his career as Asst. Lecturer and gradually rose to the position of Principal in the Department of Technical Education. He has worked as Principal of RBVRR Institute of Technology, Jyothishmathi College of Engineering, Dean of Academics,Hi tech College of Engg.&Tech;,Director of Sri Indu Group of Educational Institutions. Presently he is working as Dean (Academics) at Kshatriya College of Engineering, Armoor, Nizamabad.

Prof. Rama Rao served ISTE AP Section as State Managing Committee member from 1997 to 1998, as National Council Member from 1999 to 2002 and from 2006 to 2011. He was the Hon. Secretary of ISTE AP Section from 2003 to 2014
